# DTF tier manifest: conda-cep47-coverage  (artifact-keeper#6530)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams.mock-conda (its `/gate/`
# channel: dtfgate-old carries an upstream indexed_timestamp, dtfgate-noidx
# none).
#
# COVERAGE for CEP 47 `indexed_timestamp` beyond the hosted/virtual
# repodata.json cases of conda-virtual-shadow-and-cache:
#   * hosted: repodata.json, .bz2, .zst, current_repodata.json and the CEP-16
#     shard carry the same indexed_timestamp, at or after the upload;
#   * promotion: a package promoted from a staging channel into a local one
#     is listed there with an indexed_timestamp;
#   * pass-through: an ungated Remote and a Virtual over it serve the
#     upstream's value unchanged (repodata.json and the synthesised shard) and
#     inject none into a record that has none;
#   * the real-client run lives in conda-age-gate: pixi solving against a
#     gated remote (pixi 0.81 does not read indexed_timestamp yet, so an
#     exclude-newer run against a hosted channel would key on the builder
#     timestamp and prove nothing about indexed_timestamp).
# Every gate is a CONTROL: green on main and on the #6526 branch.
# No COVERS: every case is a CONTROL (coverage for #6530, no fix to prove).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
